---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import news from "../../../data/news/news-2025.js";
import imgFeatured from "../../../assets/news/2025/goodbye-dakota.jpg";
import { Icon } from "astro-icon/components";
import { ViewTransitions } from "astro:transitions";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

const article = news[0];
const { author, title, content, img, date, id } = article;
---

<ViewTransitions />
<Layout title=`${title} - Fallen Oak`>
  <div
    class="bg-[#fefce8] min-h-[calc(100vh-10rem)] px-4 lg:px-0 flex flex-col items-center"
  >
    <a
      class="mt-24 duration-300 hover:bg-blue-200 bg-blue-50 border-2 border-blue-200 hover:border-blue-400 rounded font-semibold text-base px-3 py-1 flex items-center gap-x-2"
      href="../"
      ><Icon name="mdi:arrow-back" class="text-2xl text-blue-600" />Back to News</a
    >
    <div class="w-full lg:w-1/2 mx-auto py-8">
      <article class="px-6 mx-auto flex flex-col lg:flex-col gap-x-12 gap-y-8">
        <div class="flex justify-center w-full lg:w-full">
          <Image 
          transition:name={id} src={imgFeatured} alt="News" width="400" class="object-cover w-auto h-64 border-2 rounded border-black" />
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-8 w-full lg:w-full">
          <div class="flex flex-col mx-auto gap-y-2 w-full">
            <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-semibold leading-none whitespace-wrap">{title}</h1>
            <p class="text-xs lg:text-sm">
              by
              <span class="text-blue-400">
                <span>{author}</span>
              </span>on
              <time datetime="2021-02-12 15:34:18-0200">{date}</time>
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4 lg:text-base text-sm rounded border border-dashed border-black p-4 bg-amber-100">
            <!-- <p>{content}</p> -->
            <p>It’s been a rough few days. I try to remind myself where there is pain, there is joy just around the corner.</p>
            <p>Sadly, our sweet Dakota crossed the rainbow bridge on Tuesday. Dakota was a 24-year-old Rocky Mountain horse who came into the rescue last year as a Sanctuary horse, as he had DSLD. The past month he was starting to show signs of pain, and his back left pastern was very close to the ground. Dr. Knowles and I agreed it was better to let him go on a good day before the ligament got worse. It’s never easy making these decisions, but I will always do what’s best for the horses.</p>
            <p>Run free, sweet boy. Tell Montana I miss her.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
